  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications:  A01 (Rev B), A02 (Rev B), A03, E00, E01, E02, E03, E04, P01 (Rev B), P02 (Rev B), P03 (Rev A), P04  Received:  19 August 2026.  \r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - No additional windows or openings shall be formed in the rear and side elevations of the development hereby permitted.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The additional ground floor side window within the building's southern ground floor side wall hereby permitted shall be obscure glazed, non-openable (excluding trickle vents within its frame) below 1.7 metres above finished floor level and be permanently retained as such.  \r\n\r\nReasons:  To protect neighbour privacy and prevent overlooking.  "
  ],
